    },
    "limitations": [
     "The original figure gave no citation for this statement. 4UN3 is the PAM-complex structure and is a likely source, but no attribution is made here."
    ]
   },
   "c_scaffold": {
    "statement": "The crRNA:tracrRNA scaffold forms a repeat:anti-repeat duplex with tetraloop and stem loops 1–3, accommodated on the REC surface.",
    "kind": "established",
    "describes": [
     {
      "type": "entity",
      "id": "sgrna"
     }
    ],
    "sourceIds": [],
    "context": {
     "species": "Streptococcus pyogenes"
    }
   },
   "c_rloop_formation": {
    "statement": "The guide RNA spacer base-pairs with the target strand over 20 nucleotides, displacing the non-target strand to form an R-loop.",
    "kind": "established",
    "describes": [
     {
      "type": "relationship",
      "id": "r_loop_formation"
     },
     {
      "type": "entity",
      "id": "non_target_strand"
     }
    ],
    "sourceIds": [],
    "context": {
     "species": "Streptococcus pyogenes"
    }
   },
   "c_rloop_allostery": {
    "statement": "Complete 20-nt R-loop propagation acts as an allosteric switch that moves the HNH domain (about 180° rotation, about 30 Å) from an inactive checkpoint conformation onto the target-strand scissile phosphate.",
    "kind": "established",
    "describes": [
     {
      "type": "entity",
      "id": "hnh_domain"
     },
     {
      "type": "entity",
      "id": "r_loop"
     },
     {
      "type": "relationship",
      "id": "rloop_activates_hnh"
     }
    ],
    "sourceIds": [
     "sternberg2015",
     "dagdas2017"
    ],
    "context": {
     "species": "Streptococcus pyogenes",
     "method": "single-molecule FRET; cryo-EM (as stated by the original figure)"
    },
    "limitations": [
     "Sources were changed from the original figure's citations (see sources[].note); whether they support the specific magnitudes (about 180°, about 30 Å) has not been checked."
    ]
   },
   "c_seed_mismatch": {
    "statement": "Mismatches in the PAM-proximal seed region (positions 1–8) stall R-loop propagation, prevent REC3 distortion and trap HNH in an inactive state, which prevents cleavage.",
    "kind": "established",
    "describes": [
     {
      "type": "entity",
      "id": "seed_mismatch"
     },
     {
      "type": "relationship",
      "id": "mismatch_blocks_hnh"
     }
    ],
    "sourceIds": [
     "szczelkun2014"
    ],
    "context": {
     "species": "Streptococcus pyogenes"
    },
    "limitations": [
     "The cited paper is about R-loop formation; whether it supports the REC3 and HNH-trapping part of the statement is unchecked. The original text also says this 'terminates off-target DNA cleavage', which is a stronger claim than 'prevents cleavage in this state'."
    ]
   },
   "c_catalytic_cleavage": {
    "statement": "RuvC (Asp10, Glu762, His983, Asp986) cleaves the non-target strand and HNH (Asp839, His840, Asn863) cleaves the target strand, each 3 nt from the PAM, producing a blunt double-strand break.",
    "kind": "established",
    "describes": [
     {
      "type": "relationship",
      "id": "ruvc_cleaves_nts"
     },
     {
      "type": "relationship",
      "id": "hnh_cleaves_ts"
     }
    ],
    "sourceIds": [
     "jinek2012"
    ],
    "context": {
     "species": "Streptococcus pyogenes"
    },
    "limitations": [
     "Per-residue assignments (for example His983 and Asn863) were not checked against the cited source."
    ]
   },
   "c_mismatch_illustration": {
    "statement": "In this figure a seed mismatch limits pairing to 6 of 20 nucleotides and keeps HNH undocked; the extent of pairing is a teaching simplification.",
    "kind": "illustrative",
    "describes": [
     {
      "type": "relationship",
      "id": "mismatch_blocks_hnh"
     }
    ],
    "sourceIds": []
   },
   "c_timeline_illustration": {
    "statement": "The 9 s timeline and its phases (pairing from 8% to 56%, HNH docking from 52% to 76%, cleavage after 82%) form a teaching sequence, not measured kinetics.",
    "kind": "illustrative",
    "describes": [],
    "sourceIds": []
   }
  }
